2394               /      ROUTINE TO SCAN A TEXT LINE FOR KEYWORD DELIMITERS.
2395               
2396               /       THIS  ROUTINE EXPECTS THE AC TO POINT TO A TEXT LINE TO  SCAN  AND  FINDS  THE
2397               /       FIRST NON-SPACE, NON-END OF LINE CHAR IN THE LINE AND SETS "SCAN1" TO POINT TO
2398               /       IT.  NEXT WE FIND THE LAST CHAR IN THE LINE THAT IS A  NON-SPACE,  NON-END  OF
2399               /       LINE  AND  STORE  A  POINTER  TO  IT  IN "SCAN2".  KEYWORDS ARE DELIMITED BY A
2400               /       BEGINNING OF  LINE  OR SPACE AT THE BEGINNING AND AN END OF LINE OR A SPACE AT
2401               /       THE END.
2402               
2403               /       ENTER:  AC = POINTER TO COMMAND LINE
2404               
2405               /       EXIT: (SUCCESS) SCAN1 = POINTER TO FIRST CHAR OF KEYWORD.
2406               /                       SCAN2 = POINTER TO LAST CHAR OF KEYWORD.
2407               /                       RETURN = RETURN + 2 (NO WORDS LEFT IN LINE).
2408               
2409               /       EXIT: (FAIL)    RETURN = RETURN + 1.
2410               
