3086               /      ROUTINE TO COMPARE TWO FILE NAMES FOR EQUALITY.
3087               /       THE ROUTINE WILL CHECK EACH OF THE 8 FILE NAME CHARS AND IF A
3088               /       CHAR IN THE FIRST FILE NAME (THE ONE WE ARE LOOKING FOR) CONTAINS
3089               /       A "?" IT WILL MATCH ON THE SECOND FILE NAME CHAR.
3090               /       ENTER WITH "FCMP1" POINTING TO THE FILE NAME TO FIND, AND "FCMP2"
3091               /       POINTING TO THE FILE NAME TO TRY AND MATCH.  EXIT + 1 IF NO MATCH
3092               /       AND EXIT + 2 IF MATCH.  (IF NON-ZERO AC ON ENTRY, THE AC IS ASSUMED
3093               /       TO HAVE THE VALUE FOR "FCMP2".)
